  "description": "500W Rear Hub Motor with 860W Peak\n\nThe Epik Swan runs on a 500W brushless geared rear hub motor that surges up to 860W peak when the terrain demands it. It delivers quiet, smooth power assist whether you're climbing a hill or cruising through city streets — giving you the confidence to tackle any route without worrying about running out of juice.\n\n48V Samsung Cell Battery\n\nPowered by a 48V 11Ah lithium-ion battery built with trusted Samsung 18650 cells, the Epik Swan delivers up to 40 miles of range per charge. Samsung cells are chosen for their consistency, safety, and long cycle life — so you get reliable performance ride after ride, not just when the battery is new.\n\nFolding Step-Through Frame\n\nThe Epik Swan's step-through frame makes mounting and dismounting effortless for riders of all ages and mobility levels. When you're done riding, it folds down compactly for easy storage in tight apartments, car trunks, or office spaces — combining accessibility and portability in one clean design.\n\nAlloy Hydraulic Disc Brakes\n\nFront and rear alloy hydraulic disc brakes give the Epik Swan precise, powerful stopping in any condition. Hydraulic systems self-adjust over time and require minimal maintenance compared to mechanical brakes — so you get consistent, fade-free performance without having to think about it.\n\nKenda Puncture-Resistant Tires\n\nThe 20\" x 2.125\" Kenda K-924 tires are built with puncture-resistant construction to keep you rolling through glass, gravel, and debris that would flatten a standard tire. Designed for urban and mixed-terrain riding, they provide reliable grip and durability so flat tires don't cut your commute short.",
